  "review": "Additive host resolveNoteTarget callback maps monophonic aliases to a canonical physical voice owner for Stop Loop. Default callback retains the existing integer-channel ownership behavior. No audio rendering, chip register transforms, clock/parser/DSP/WASM or gains change. Both canonical and served copies must be identical. Differential default-behavior and explicit alias-ownership regressions are executed without audio devices.",
